I picked up my Tesla Model Y at the dealership today, whole thing took me 5 minutes, popped it in full self driving to see how it would do on busy Miami streets in the rain. 

I am not making this up, 10 minutes into my drive a lunatic (this is Miami after all) tried to merge into my lane without looking; the Tesla nimbly swerved and made room. Don't know if I would have been able to react. 70% sure it would have been a collision had I been driving.

Pretty remarkable stuff.

I'm not saying this to glaze Tesla or anything I've never actually been a fan of the cars and I don't like the aesthetic at all or the build quality; I bought the Y entirely for FSD. And now having used it I feel like it's a completely transformative driving experience and I can never go back to ordinary cars. It's really quite something

